// Scene UV seen through the `distortion` input: its texel is the summed sample offset of this frame's distortion-pass
// draws in framebuffer pixels (+x right, +y down). Zero or non-finite offsets return uv itself, so undistorted pixels
// keep the bit-exact scene paths.
// Requires: the ShaderPackUniforms block `ubo` declared before this include.
vec2 lumenRefractedUv(sampler2D distortionImage, vec2 uv)
{
    vec2 offsetPixels = texture(distortionImage, uv).rg;
    if (any(isnan(offsetPixels)) || any(isinf(offsetPixels))) return uv;
    return clamp(uv + offsetPixels * ubo.ScreenAndMapSize.xy, vec2(0.0), vec2(1.0));
}

#ifdef RIMLUMEN_PACK_UNIFORMS_INCLUDED
// UV for every screen-aligned input a composite puts over the scene (hdr, bloom, a pack's own layers such as streaks):
// sceneUv while the player setting "distortion also refracts RimLumen effects" is on, so effects bend with the scene
// behind them, else uv. Defined only when the block comes from PostFx/RimLumenPackUniforms.glslinc (224 bytes, with
// LayerFlags). A pack that declares its own 208-byte block or samples only `scene` at sceneUv still compiles and runs;
// its layer simply stays unrefracted.
vec2 lumenLayerUv(vec2 uv, vec2 sceneUv)
{
    return ubo.LayerFlags.x > 0.5 ? sceneUv : uv;
}
#endif
